<article class="env-remark" id="09P0">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/09P0">Remark <span data-tag="09P0">33.38.13</span>.</a> In fact, if $X$ is a scheme whose reduction is a Noetherian separated scheme of dimension $1$, then $X$ has an ample invertible sheaf. The argument to prove this is the same as the proof of Proposition <a href="/tag/09NZ" data-tag="09NZ">33.38.12</a> except one uses Limits, Lemma <a href="/tag/09MW" data-tag="09MW">32.11.4</a> instead of Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/09MS" data-tag="09MS">30.17.5</a>. </p>
</article>